````markdown
# Third ways for a portable TW5 engine: the map after the rulings

Lares (Artificer) · Fable, tasked spirit · 2026-10-16, third authoring. This version re-authors the whole map under the operator's rulings of 2026-10-16 and the floor's later frames; it replaces, rather than amends, the two earlier drafts of the same day (the last kept as `third-ways.prev-2026-10-16.md`). Inputs read whole: the boot seed; the six sibling reports in this folder (`model-and-gaps.md`, `portable-engine-plan.md`, `portable-engine-plan-v2.md`, `host-attractors.md`, `mudlet-capabilities.md`, `evaluators-one-or-many.md`); the house memes `dreamdom.mem` (#/the-ruling, #/the-layers), `page-controls.mem`, `wikispace-canvasspace-ontology.mem`, `recipe-layer-model.mem`, `wiki-layer-ontology.mem`, `render-pipeline.mem`, `memetic-wikitext.mem` (#/processing-model, #/conformance, Annex B), `mudlet-scout.mem`, `evaluators-one-or-many.mem`. Code opened where a claim leans on it: `TiddlyWiki5/core/ui/RootTemplate.tid`, `core/modules/startup/render.js`, `core/modules/widgets/widget.js`, `core/modules/utils/fakedom.js`; `packages/lararium-tw5/src/tw5-camera.ts`, `tw5-projection.ts`, `outbound-bridge.ts`, `sovereign-kernel.ts`; `packages/lararium-web/src/projection-sink.ts`. Nothing edited, nothing booted.

**Reach.** This pass ran no web search and no web fetch; every web-sourced claim carries the mark the earlier pass gave it, with "prior pass" added. Marks: **[reached: fetched]** page or file read in a session of this thread · **[reached: search]** confirmed only through a search passage · **[unreached]** memory, flagged where used · **[reached: code]** read in `/home/user/gjd5` this pass · *(inferred)* reasoning, not evidence. Claims resting on a sibling report name it.

**Vocabulary.** *Store* = the CRDT, one Automerge document per bag, the virtual backend. *Engine* = the headless TW5 VM: parser, filters, widget tree, actions, wiki state; the reference evaluator of the wiki language. *Projection* = any surface read by a human or a program. *Sensorium* = the perception capability that turns a raw river into typed percepts. *Camera* = one root template rendered into one document sink. *Keyed absolute frame* = the whole rendered state of one named key with its own monotone revision, droppable and self-healing (`dreamdom.mem#/the-ruling`). *Record* = one whole tiddler, keyed by title. *Actor* = one wiki's engine, addressed by id, one writer, able to hibernate.

---

## 1. Summary and recommendation

The operator asked for the paths beyond two. The map now holds **one architecture with two settings and one lifecycle**, and the rest of the field folds into it as contract lines or stands rejected by name.

1. **Four layers, two waists, two grains.** STORE / ENGINE / PROJECTIONS out / SENSORIA in. The store↔engine waist carries **records** (whole tiddlers, tombstones, cursors). The engine↔projection waist carries **keyed absolute rendered frames** at the grain each camera declares at mount: a Story River frame, a canvas shape, a Mudlet pane's declared key, each carrying its whole rendered state with transclusions resolved (kahea followed live, aka kept frozen) and its affordances inside the key. Writes travel as writes, never as events. The sensorium enters the engine through a capability gate, as writes or verbs with an actor, only on vessels that carry its dependencies. (§2)

2. **A camera = (root template, document sink).** TW5's widget tree writes to whatever implements the document interface; `$tw.fakeDocument` proves it upstream and the house's `mountCamera(engine, {rootTiddler, document, container})` already takes `window.document` or a fake document as a parameter **[reached: code]**. `$:/core/ui/RootTemplate` transcludes whatever `$:/layout` names and falls back to `$:/core/ui/PageTemplate` **[reached: code]**. So the page template over the browser DOM stands as the browser's first camera, and a blocks sink, a text sink, a canvas sink or a Mudlet pane sink each stand as another root over another document. The engine need not sit in the app for a camera to exist there: a sink beside the engine emits whole keys across the wire. (§2.3)

3. **The Replica Port family, one port with a width dial.** v1's Candidate C (engine twin on the glass) and the earlier E (filter port) merge: a projection subscribes at a width, **full → skinny → story → none**. At full, skinny and story the projection hosts a second engine fed at record grain and mounts its own camera in-process. At none the engine stays headless and a camera mounted beside it ships keyed rendered frames to a sink that cannot run the engine. The dial moves *where the engine↔projection waist sits*; it never moves the store↔engine waist. (§4.1)

4. **The Wiki Actor sets the lifecycle.** One id, one writer, hibernation, a capability manifest. Actor states on the first surface: **daemon** always awake; **pinned** awake while it holds a glass slot; **sleeping** = store persisted, engine cold; **recipe** = a bag stack with no actor yet; **spawn** = boot the engine over the stack and mount the page template as root. (§3)

5. **The first surface**: the browser on the same box as the Node vessel, holding the daemon wiki, a pinned wiki, and other wikis available as recipes or sleeping actors, each spawning in the browser as the ordinary TW5 page template with house customizations. The Node question answers inside this frame: one engine per wiki in a `worker_thread`, the browser page as the glass, synchronous asks available on Node alone. (§3)

6. **Rejected, named once, not re-argued**: the TW5 syncer and any syncadaptor facade (web-2.5 design; adaptors bind the wiki `change` event directly with an origin-tagged echo guard); mutation-log and DOM-delta streams across any waist (Candidate B, "the mutators"); the store-only worker as a sole-engine design (no engine on Lua 5.1, no store on Hermes or QuickJS without WASM); the Lockstep Twin (TW5 stamps `modified` and reads clocks). (§4.0)

7. **Q1 closed**: one pinned JS TW5 reference evaluator for the full dialects; an evaluator-neutral conformance suite built now with that engine as oracle; the parse tree normative, per-camera serialisation second; a certified core-subset evaluator only when a host earns it; Mudlet receives results, never the language. *"The language carries portability; its suite carries the language."* (§6)

**Recommendation.** Build the Replica Port with its dial and the Wiki Actor around it, in this order: (a) the record-grain port inside the engine with `width`, `causedBy` and the presence lane (v2 Phase 1); (b) the keyed-frame camera contract hardened by `page-controls.mem` so width-none sinks (the current DOM sink, a blocks sink, Mudlet's pane) emit and consume whole keys with declared cancellation and a frame resend; (c) the glass engine behind a flag at full and skinny widths; (d) the actor lifecycle (hibernate, wake, manifest) over all of it; (e) `filter-cts.json` and the camera goldens so every host answers a published row. One spike separates the live options: the same 2,000-tiddler corpus booted three times over one loopback port at full, skinny and none, measured in §10.

**What this version changed against the previous one.** The earlier drafts carried a "what changed" ledger and treated C and E as rivals, F as a live candidate, the Node question as a separate chapter, and the lean-host notch as "blocks per tiddler". This version removes the ledger, merges C and E on the dial, demotes F to a measurement inside the spike, folds Node into the first-surface section, replaces "blocks per tiddler" with keyed rendered frames at camera grain, adds the actor states, the camera-as-root-plus-sink reading, the closed Q1, and the six-line moʻolelo draft (§12).

---

## 2. The frame

### 2.1 Four layers

| Layer | Holds | Never holds | House code today (survey) |
|---|---|---|---|
| **STORE** | truth: one Automerge doc per bag; composite layers (canon ← working ← personal ← draft ← temp, `recipe-layer-model.mem#/as-mounted`); residency; the disk projection as a one-way mirror | a rendered form; a DOM; a percept at river grain | `sovereign-kernel.ts`, `CompositeStore`, `IslandAdaptor`, `WaveLanding`, `disk-projector.ts` |
| **ENGINE** | the TW5 VM: parser, filters, widget tree, actions, `$tw.wiki` as a materialised cache; the reference evaluator | truth (it reads and writes the store); a caret; geometry | `TW5Engine.boot`, the third-runtime forge (`$tw.browser = $tw.node = null`), `outbound-bridge.ts` bound to `change` |
| **PROJECTIONS (out)** | cameras: a root template over a document sink; the river it chooses; the control a human holds | truth; sensoria; authority | `tw5-camera.ts`, `tw5-projection.ts`, `projection-sink.ts` |
| **SENSORIA (in)** | the perception machina: capture, structure, worldline; percepts typed from a river | the river itself in the store; a projection's input semantics | `@lararium/sensorium` (manifest read; code not) |

The sensorium stands as a **capability**: a vessel that lacks its dependencies still stands as a lararium and says so in its manifest. Live 3D games wait on the sensorium finishing; this lane stays on TiddlyWiki integration.

Field precedents for the first three layers, from the prior pass: CQRS and event sourcing; Datomic's storage / peer / application **[reached: search, prior pass]**; Croquet's log / model / view **[reached: fetched, prior pass]**; Zero's Postgres / zero-cache / client and LiveStore's log / materializer / query **[reached: fetched and search, prior pass]**. For the fourth layer the field offers halves only: lockstep netcode's *inputs cross, state never does* **[reached: search, prior pass]** and MCP's *acts arrive named as tool calls* (`host-attractors.md` §1.4).

### 2.2 Two waists, two grains

**Store↔engine, at record grain.** The engine reads the composite store and writes back through the `change` listener: `bridgeWikiToAdaptor` skips foam the LandedLedger just landed, HandGate paces at 400 ms trailing / 2 s cap, the in-wiki `bag-paths` cascade routes by kind (survey §3.2; `outbound-bridge.ts` **[reached: code]**). Every TW5 engine already emits one batched change set per tick, keyed by title with `modified`/`deleted` flags and a per-title `changeCount` (`wiki.js` **[reached: fetched, prior pass]**). Tombstones explicit; cursors monotone; a write carries a `txId` and gets an answer (v2 P2, P14). **No syncer stands between.** The adaptor on either side of any record stream binds the `change` event directly and lands inbound records under an origin stamp its own listener skips; TW5-Yjs's origin-tagged `transact` and TidGi's titles-in-flight check supply the echo discipline, their syncer facades do not travel (v2 §0.3–0.5 **[reached: fetched, prior pass]**).

**Engine↔projection, at rendered-key grain.** The operator's correction stands: "whole blocks per tiddler" read as missing context. The grain follows `dreamdom.mem#/the-ruling` (2026-10-11): a camera's surface divides into keys; each key carries its **whole rendered state** and its own revision; the grain rides the camera and gets declared at mount; the frustum culls; membership stands as a key of its own; one writer per key; each frame names the sensed revision it took in; only true events queue and each gets an answer. A Story River keys by tiddler frame with the river order as a key; a canvas keys by shape; a Mudlet pane keys by the key it declared. Inside each key: transclusions resolved (kahea followed live, aka kept frozen, `render-pipeline.mem#/render-posture`), and the key's affordances (the acts its widgets would fire, as handles). TW5's own `refresh(changedTiddlers)` maps record changes to dirty widgets, and the widget tree answers "which keys changed" without any diff of the document **[reached: code, `widget.js:764`]**. So a sink beside the engine still emits **whole keys, never DOM edits**.

**Sensorium↔engine, through the gate.** A percept arrives as `port:write{records}` or `port:ask{kind:"verb"}` with the river's actor, and passes the capability the vessel declared. The raw river never enters the store at line grain; `mudlet-capabilities.md` §4.1 puts it in a session log beside the island with digests promoted by verb.

**A fourth boundary that must not exist**: projection↔sensorium. A thing that writes back for a human reads as a projection; a thing that writes back for a river reads as a sensorium; the store should know which actor spoke.

### 2.3 A camera = (root template, document sink)

The operator's frame (Telarus, verbatim, quote license): *"The TW5 architecture really allows ANY template or root->widget-tree to serve as a render target. The DOM stack just serves as Jeremy's most pono browser projection. In other stacks with different capabilities, we can leverage this, even if the engine doesn't sit in the app (Mudlet)."*

What the code says in support:

- `startup/render.js` builds the page widget with `makeTranscludeWidget(PAGE_TEMPLATE_TITLE, {document: document, parentWidget: $tw.rootWidget})` and the title and stylesheet widgets with `{document: $tw.fakeDocument}` in the same file: the document arrives as a parameter, never as an architecture **[reached: code, lines 30–66]**.
- Every widget holds `this.document = options.document` and creates its nodes through it (`widget.js:39`, `:934`) **[reached: code]**.
- `RootTemplate.tid` reads `<$transclude tiddler={{{ [{$:/layout}has[text]] ~[[$:/core/ui/PageTemplate]] }}} mode="inline"/>` followed by `{{$:/core/ui/Confirmations}}`: the layout switcher stands as a root tiddler that composes a surface, which `dreamdom.mem#/the-layers` already reads as the view frustum in a root **[reached: code]**.
- `fakedom.js` (372 lines) supplies `setAttribute`, `innerHTML` serialisation, and an `addEventListener` the house patches to stamp render ids; it carries `isTiddlyWikiFakeDom = true` so five core sites degrade on purpose (`dreamdom.mem#/what-a-replacement-un-skips`) **[reached: code]**.
- The house's `mountCamera` takes `{rootTiddler, document: TW5FakeDocument | Document, container}`, renders once, and refreshes on `change`; its own comment reads "Isomorphic — works with window.document (browser), $tw.fakeDocument (Node/SSR), or any fake-DOM implementation" **[reached: code, `tw5-camera.ts:26–75`]**.

Consequences. (i) **The page template over `window.document` stands as the browser's first camera**, and spawning a wiki in the browser means booting its engine and mounting that root. (ii) A **blocks sink** reads as a document implementation that records elements and attributes as a small tree and serialises affordances from the listeners the widgets bind; a **text sink** and a **label-html sink** (Mudlet's Qt subset) read as serialisers over the same tree; a **canvas sink** reads as the DreamDOM document `wikispace-canvasspace-ontology.mem#/the-surface-law` already demands (DOM-hosting, never rasterising). (iii) **Layer 3 belongs to the page** wherever a page exists: editors, popups, scrolling, drag and drop, file browsing stay out of the island's camera and get supplied by page-native controls named in the template (`page-controls.mem`), or refuse by name. (iv) Annex B's pending `resolveWidgetTree(ast, registry)` names the middle layer the blocks sink needs for memetic-wikitext specifically (`memetic-wikitext.mem#/annex-open` **[reached: code]**).

### 2.4 Co-location against blur

A thread may host more than one layer. The test: **does the co-located copy own anything its layer should not?** A glass engine that renders from a record-grain replica owns no truth (the store↔engine waist stays in the worker), no sensoria, no authority (writes carry the human as actor and pass the gate in the worker): co-location. A glass engine that holds `$:/state` the worker needs, evaluates verbs the worker cannot, or ingests a river: blur. The actor manifest (§3) makes the test mechanical.

---

## 3. The actor lifecycle and the first surface

### 3.1 Actor states

| State | Store | Engine | Camera | Transition |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **daemon** | persisted, fleet-synced; `wikis/daemon/working` late-attached as its write layer (`wiki-layer-ontology.mem#/the-daemon-wiki`) | always awake | mounted when summoned (Ctrl+Shift+D, ☰) | never hibernates |
| **pinned** | persisted | awake | holds a glass slot (the vessel's default pinned primary wiki, `lares`-as-wiki by ruling) | hibernates only when unpinned and its last attachment goes quiet |
| **sleeping** | persisted | cold | none | wake on `open`; per-port attachments restored |
| **recipe** | a bag stack named in a record; no doc opened for the wiki's slots yet | none | none | spawn: resolve slot docs, boot the engine over the stack, mount the root |
| **spawned** | as pinned or sleeping | awake | the page template over the browser DOM, with house customisations | becomes pinned when it takes a slot, sleeping when it loses its last attachment |

The field supplies the shape: Cloudflare Durable Objects, single-threaded, one id, transactional storage only the object touches, hibernation that drops memory while connections stay, per-connection attachments serialised and restored **[reached: fetched, docs via GitHub, prior pass]**; Spritely Goblins vats and CapTP references **[reached: search, prior pass]**; BEAM supervisors **[reached: search, prior pass]**. The Smalltalk image and Node's `v8.startupSnapshot` (stable since 22.17/24.0; serialize and deserialize hooks; no re-snapshot of a deserialized app; workers unmentioned) name what a sleeping actor's warm start could become **[reached: fetched, prior pass]** *(inferred: untested in a `Worker`)*.

What hibernation demands: everything a projection depends on must fit in its attachment, `{cursor, subscriptions, width, actorKey, localFilter, cameraMount}`. Today's engine-side `$:/state`, the confirm road's `$:/temp/confirm/*`, and the projection's rid map all live in the engine heap; the Replica Port moves `$:/state`, StoryList, HistoryList, temp and `$:/info/browser/*` to the glass by the tier filter (v2 P10), and the keyed-frame camera makes the rid map a cursored lease that dies with the render (`host-attractors.md` §2.4). The capability gate the house already wants (replacing `worker-trust`, survey gap #16) lands on the actor by design. A percept addressed to an actor whose manifest lacks `sensoria` answers `refused: cap sensoria` by name.

### 3.2 The first surface: the browser on the Node vessel's box

The browser opens against the Node vessel on the same machine. It shows the daemon wiki, the pinned wiki, and a list of other wikis, each in one of the states above. Opening a recipe spawns an actor; opening a sleeping actor wakes it; both mount the TW5 page template with house customisations as the browser camera. Where that engine runs (in the page, in a `worker_thread` with a replica in the page, or in a worker with a frame sink in the page) reads as the width dial of §4.1, measured rather than ruled.

**The Node question, answered inside this frame.** "One in main and one in each wiki worker thread… not great on Node?" On Node the main thread holds no document, so its projection roles read: a CLI that tails, writes and asks; an SSR face that renders through the fakedom camera; a relay (behind the causal-island boundary). None needs a second engine *for interaction*. The honest shape: one engine per wiki in a `worker_thread` with `resourceLimits` as the eviction tripwire; main holds a port client and, for SSR, a render-only camera over the fakedom document. TidGi-Desktop runs exactly the hosting half of this in production (a Node TiddlyWiki inside a `worker_thread`, a browser TiddlyWiki in the renderer, tiddlers crossing) **[reached: fetched, prior pass]**; the house keeps the hosting and drops the adaptor. Node gives one thing browsers refuse: the main thread may block on `Atomics.wait`, so a `port:ask{kind:"filter"}` can run *synchronously* inside a TW5 filter run, which synckit proves at about 0.14 ms a round trip (`Atomics.wait` + `receiveMessageOnPort`) **[reached: fetched, prior pass]**. That makes the skinny notch cheaper to prove on Node first *(inferred: bounded waits only)*. Node stays weaker on multi-tab (no Web Locks; G's one-writer-per-actor makes election moot), Bun's `worker_threads` stands partial and Deno's **[unreached]**. Sensoria live most naturally here, since a Node vessel carries file watchers, sockets and native modules a tab or a Lua client cannot.

Two engines on one box therefore read as normal, not as a smell: the daemon's actor and a pinned wiki's actor already stand as two engines in the Node vessel today; the browser adds a camera to each, and a replica engine beside the camera only where the dial says it pays.

---

## 4. Families, re-scored after the rulings

### 4.0 Rejected or folded, named once

| Family | Status | Why, in one line |
|---|---|---|
| TW5 syncer / syncadaptor facade | **rejected (operator)** | web-2.5 design: a task queue, a 1 s throttle, a 60 s poll, one-at-a-time saves, no tombstones, no conflict logic (`syncer.js` **[reached: fetched, prior pass]**); adaptors bind `change` directly with an origin-tagged echo guard |
| B, mutation-log / DOM-delta twin ("the mutators") | **rejected (operator)** | a delta must queue and cannot drop; dropping corrupts silently (`dreamdom.mem#/the-fork`); frames stay keyed absolute |
| F, store-only worker as sole engine | **fails** | no engine on Mudlet (Lua 5.1 exact **[reached: fetched, sibling]**), Verse, Discord or MCP; no store on Hermes or QuickJS (no `WebAssembly` **[reached: fetched and search, sibling]**); no TW5 parser port in any language in twenty years (`evaluators-one-or-many.md`); survives as the verb census inside the spike |
| Lockstep Twin (Croquet / Multisynq, GGPO) | **not spiked** | TW5 stamps `modified`, reads `Date`, uses random ids; Croquet bans those in model code **[reached: fetched, prior pass]**; its lesson (inputs cross, state never does) goes to the sensorium seam; a pinned wiki as snapshot + cursor goes to the actor |
| Resumable Widget Tree (Qwik, Marko, RSC Flight) | **folded** | ship-the-tree-with-declared-listeners names the blocks sink's serialisation and the `data-lar-on`/`data-lar-cancel` stamps; resumption of TW5's widget tree stays unbuilt |
| Hypermedia and server-driven UI (LiveView, Hotwire, Hyperview) | **folded** | reads as the width-none notch served to a rich DOM; its one law, *the focused control belongs to the human*, lives in `page-controls.mem` and in every port adaptor |
| Namespace as interface (Plan 9 / 9P) | **folded** | the Node and CLI face of the port: `/wikis/<slug>/tiddlers/<title>`, `/filters/<f>`, `/render/<title>.<target>`, `/ctl`, `/events`; the disk projection already stands as half of it, one way |
| The image (Smalltalk, Lively, the single-file TW5) | **folded** | the sleeping actor's warm start; `v8.startupSnapshot` as a real mechanism |
| Host contract as a declared world (WIT, Extism) | **folded** | the engine's host floor (`host-attractors.md` §2.1) and the language's conformance classes read as one instrument seen from two sides (§6) |
| Dataflow and signals (Observable, HyperFormula) | **folded** | TW5 refresh already runs as a dataflow with per-tick batching; the Replica Port's propagation rule: a filter with no observer never runs |
| Headless content, one runtime behind many surfaces (ink, Yarn Spinner, headless CMS) | **folded** | ink ports its evaluator because its language stays small; the house ports rendered keys because its evaluator reads as TW5 and no second one exists **[reached: search, sibling]** |

### 4.1 The Replica Port family — one port, a width dial

*Plain words.* A projection opens a port and declares a width. At **full**, the projection hosts a second TW5 engine fed every record and every field; it renders its own camera in-process, over `window.document`. At **skinny**, the same, but records carry titles, `tags`, `modified`, `type`, `caption` for everything and full text only for subscribed filters and open tiddlers; a touch of unsubscribed text asks the engine (`port:ask{kind:"load"}`), synchronously on Node, asynchronously with a re-render in a browser. At **story**, skinny plus the open story and the sidebar's live filters at open. At **none**, the projection hosts no engine; a camera mounted beside the headless engine renders the projection's declared root into a sink and ships keyed absolute frames at the grain declared at mount, with affordances inside each key; acts come back as `wiki:control-event`-shaped writes or invokes with an id and get an answer.

*What moves with the dial, and what never does.* Full, skinny and story move the record-grain stream across the thread to a second engine and keep the rendered-key waist in-process. None keeps the record stream inside the worker and moves the rendered-key waist across the thread. **The store↔engine waist never moves**: truth stays in the worker's composite store under every setting, and the glass engine owns none of it.

*Field.* TW5 itself proves the skinny/full split inside its renderer: `lazy-all` holds skinny tiddlers and loads text when `getTiddlerText` touches it, with known holes in export, `$text` on a skinny tiddler and JS modules **[reached: fetched (syncer source) and search, prior pass]**. Zero replicates subsets of rows per query and keeps them current by incremental view maintenance; LiveStore materialises an event log into per-tab SQLite and re-runs reactive queries; Datomic peers embed the index and subscribe to the transactor's log; Observable computes a variable only when something observes it **[reached: fetched and search, prior pass]**. TidGi-Desktop and TidGi-Mobile prove the two-engine hosting on Electron and on a phone (30,000 tiddlers: 5 s from SQLite plus 5 s for indexers; loading ~300 recent cut 10 s to 5 s) **[reached: fetched and search, prior pass]**, which says TW5's startup indexers, not the port, set the phone's boot number and the skinny notch exists for that.

*Layers and waists.* STORE and ENGINE in the worker at every width. PROJECTION on the glass with a co-located render engine at full/skinny/story and none at width none. Blur check: passes while the glass engine holds no truth, no sensoria, no authority; returns the moment a verb runs on the glass against a skinny replica without an ask (the `lazy-all` export hole in layer terms).

*Known as-built gaps, placed.* At full, skinny and story the HIGH list dissolves because the handler runs beside a real control: #23 textarea revert, #1 blanket click `preventDefault` (unconditional at `projection-sink.ts:199` **[reached: code]**), #4 checkbox act and radio paint, select snap-back, #2 root `tm-*` services, #13 frozen pane on switch (snapshot on `port:open`), #6 rid growth. At width none they do not dissolve; they get **answered by the camera contract**: `data-lar-on`/`data-lar-cancel` declared at binding, page-owned live controls with descriptors, `projection:resend` on a surface switch, root services registered in an island startup module or refused by name (survey §5.3; `page-controls.mem#/the-wire`, #/refusals). #3 boot-shadows pushed as one element (`sovereign-kernel.ts:405` **[reached: code]**) stays an engine fix under every width, proven green in scratch.

*Pinned, hot-swapped, multi-tab.* Hot-swap = close one port, open another; at skinny the switch cost scales with the visible story; at none it costs one fresh snapshot of keys. Pinned = the actor keeps the subscription set or the mounted camera warm. Multi-tab = one leader holds the engine, a replica or a sink per tab (v2 P15: Web Lock elects, a channel announces); a late tab gets a snapshot, never a `ready` it missed (survey gap #18).

*Cost and risk.* Full pays two cores (v1's memory falsifier). Skinny pays an IVM layer over TW5 filters (at minimum "re-run subscribed filters on the dirty set and diff", which `$list` does already) and inherits the `lazy-all` hole list; `search`, `regexp` and transclusion-dependent operators resist incrementalisation and fall back to full re-evaluation. None pays whole-key serialisation per beat (TW5's own baseline, 100–300 ms a keypress on large documents, `dreamdom.mem#/the-fork`), which the keyed grain and the frustum exist to cut, and it pays the page-controls build for every live control.

*Pattern integrity.* **A standing filter reads as a subscription; the engine owns the index, the projection owns the view; the replica's width reads as a setting, never an architecture.**

### 4.2 The keyed-frame camera — width none, read on its own

The current house projection stands here already: `tw5-projection.ts` renders RootTemplate and PageStylesheet into `$tw.fakeDocument`, coalesces at 24 ms, and emits whole HTML plus CSS; `projection-sink.ts` morphs into a shadow root **[reached: code]**. Three faults stand in it against the ruling (`page-controls.mem#/the-sink-today`): one revision orders a whole surface (no per-key revision, no mount epoch, no sensed revision); every click cancelled at handling; a stale render id answers with no event id. The rewrite under the ruling: one key per river frame plus the river order and membership, each with its revision; `sensedRevision` per control; `wiki:control-event` with an id and `projection:control-result` with a status; cancellation declared at binding; `projection:resend` on switch. Measure first: one whole-surface key stands until numbers ask for the split (`page-controls.mem#/measure-first`).

Three sinks earn names now:

| Sink | Document implementation | Serialiser | First host |
|---|---|---|---|
| DOM morph sink | the browser's shadow root, morphed per key | HTML per key, CSS as its own key | the browser at width none (today's shape, hardened) |
| blocks sink | a fakedom-style document that records element, attribute, text and bound-listener nodes | `{renderCursor, keys:[{key, rev, blocks[], affordances[]}]}`; affordance = `{id, kind: link|button|toggle|select|edit|drop, label, target?, field?}` | MCP resources, chat, UE6 sidecar panels |
| text / label-html sink | the same document | plain text; Qt's rich-text subset (`<b> <i> <u> <font color> <a href> <br> <p> <table>`) *(inferred subset, sibling)* | Mudlet labels and miniconsoles over GMCP |

An invoke carries the `renderCursor` it received; a stale one answers `stale-target`; every invoke passes the capability gate before `invokeActions`, else the lean path bypasses authority (survey gap #16). Edits never ride repeated invokes: a lean projection **reads keys and writes records** (`host-attractors.md` §2.4's correction: two read grains, one write grain). Root `tm-*` services (copy, download, print, open-window) read as host services, refused by name on hosts that lack them.

### 4.3 G, the Wiki Actor — the lifecycle layer

Already laid out in §3.1. G adds no layer and moves no waist; it wraps the engine and its store↔engine waist in a lifecycle and an authority boundary, and **exposes blur**: a projection that cannot hand back its attachment and resume after a wake holds something that belongs to the engine. Pipelining (Cap'n Proto's promise pipelining **[reached: search, prior pass]**) lets a glass do `open(wiki).ask(filter).open(firstResult)` in one round trip. *Pattern integrity:* **one object, one id, one writer, refusal by name.**

### 4.4 Two TW5 instances on one box — still an option, now a setting

The operator kept it on the table. Under this map it reads as the Replica Port at full or skinny width: the glass engine and the worker engine. It earns its keep where a human holds a rich DOM and the device has memory; it loses where the device strains (phones, TidGi-Mobile's numbers) or where no JS runs. The spike decides the default per device class; nothing here forecloses it.

---

## 5. Per-host landing

| Host | Store | Engine | Width | Camera (root → sink) | What travels | Mark |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Browser on the Node vessel's box (the first surface) | in the worker beside the Node store, synced over MessageChannel/WS | per-wiki actor in a Worker or `worker_thread` | full / skinny / story by device class; none as fallback | `$:/core/ui/RootTemplate` → `window.document` (page template with house customisations) | records at ≥ story; keyed HTML frames at none | code + survey |
| Any other browser or WebView shell | IndexedDB (evictable in Tauri/iOS shells, named as such) | actor in a Worker | same | same | same | sibling |
| Node (CLI, SSR, relay) | `storage-nodefs` | actor per wiki in `worker_thread`, `resourceLimits` | none, or a render-only camera in main for SSR | RootTemplate or a static template → `$tw.fakeDocument` | records; synchronous asks | prior pass |
| QuickJS / quickjs-ng, Hermes | **none in JS** (no WASM): store on a neighbour, or Automerge lent natively through host functions | the reference engine, ES2020 core, pump-mode timers where no `setTimeout` | the engine sits here; cameras per host | a text or blocks sink; a React Native view tree as a blocks projection | records in; keys out | sibling [reached: fetched, Hermes #429] |
| UE6 / Verse | in the sidecar | in the sidecar (Node or QuickJS); Verse's single transactional thread hosts no long-lived VM *(inferred, sibling)* | none | a blocks sink → Scene Graph entities, UMG panels | keys over `IWebSocket`; writes with the player as actor | sibling [reached: search] |
| Mudlet (Lua 5.1, no JS, no WebSocket, no listener) | in the island | in the island | none | a pane root → text / label-html sink; the pane's declared key per Geyser container | `Lar.*` GMCP packages over a loopback telnet listener (virtual-MUD pattern first, proxy second); results, never the language | sibling [reached: fetched, `CMakeLists.txt`] |
| MCP / chat | in the process | in the process | none | a resource root → blocks or text sink | resources ↔ keys; tools ↔ `port:write` / `port:ask`; the suite's `fault` names as the tool's error vocabulary | sibling [reached: fetched, MCP resources] |

Three rules ride every row: a projection declares its renders, width and limits at open; the engine emits records, keys, answers and faults, never an event; a host that lends no durable storage reads as a replica and the UI says so (`host-attractors.md` §9.2).

---

## 6. Conformance as the portability measure (Q1 closed)

The floor closed Q1 on 2026-10-16 (`evaluators-one-or-many.mem#/the-ruling`), four strokes: one reference evaluator for the full dialects, the TW5 engine in JS, wherever an engine can run; an evaluator-neutral conformance suite built now with the pinned JS engine as oracle (the sqllogictest move: run, record, review once, freeze, diff); the parse tree normative and each camera's serialisation second, with declared tolerance and mandatory degradation cases; a certified core-subset evaluator permitted only when a host proves an offline need, publishing its skip list by name ("Mustache-like" below the core). Mudlet receives results, never the language.

What this does to the map: the portability contract reads as `filter-cts.json` plus the specimen manifests and the camera goldens, and a host's conformance reads as a published row. One evaluator removes language drift and leaves host drift (`Intl`, `localeCompare`, Unicode regexp, `Date` differ between V8 and Hermes), so the suite runs per host from day one. The memetic-wikitext spec already binds the force: a vanilla TW5 engine MUST read a carrier as valid wikitext with every sigil an unbound macro call; a conforming renderer MUST target exactly one camera per pass and MAY support a subset of cameras while it MUST degrade a missing camera visibly (`#/conformance` **[reached: code]**). The camera goldens therefore start at `html` and `text`; the `blocks` golden waits on Annex B's widget-tree pass, and `label-html` derives from `blocks` after a declared projection rather than from a hand-written golden. The WIT *world* and the conformance classes read as one instrument: the world says what a host lends the evaluator, the classes say what the evaluator owes the text.

---

## 7. Mu

Seed tools: Wand `*` (visible feed, ignition), Cup `?` (macro zoom, relation), Sword `!` (micro zoom, discernment), Pentacle `_` (hidden feed, ground; presence acknowledged, essence unclaimed), Arcana `0` (unask). Conflict carries: Signal-Jam `*_`, Dubious-Move `?!`.

**Wand `*`.** Two fires. First, the code: `mountCamera` already takes the document as a parameter and `RootTemplate` already reads `$:/layout`; the camera-as-root-plus-sink reading needs no new mechanism, only a declared key grain and a second document implementation. Second, the field: every mature system moves the same thing across its boundary and it never reads as the DOM nor as a syncer's task queue; TidGi moves tiddlers, Zero rows, Croquet inputs, Durable Objects messages to one object, LiveView fragments with the focused control handed to the client, game engines the latest state per object beside one reliable event lane. The mutation stream stands as the outlier (WorkerDOM's compat table still marks `preventDefault`, `focus` and every `Selection.*` row unsupported **[reached: fetched, prior pass]**).

**Cup `?`.** Zoomed out, the families sort along two dials the house already holds: a **width dial** (full ↔ skinny ↔ story ↔ none) that places the rendered-key waist in-process or across the wire, and a **lifecycle dial** (anonymous port ↔ addressable actor with hibernation and a manifest). F sat off both because it moved the evaluator rather than the replica; the mutators cut below every waist. Seen from the Cup, a MUD already reads as a wiki with a clock (rooms as records, `look` as transclusion, `who` as presence, `mudlet-capabilities.md` §7), and a lararium joins any world as a capability with a key, never as its authority.

**Sword `!`.** Cut here: (1) between the engine's `change` event and any delivery of it (the port adaptor binds there; nothing of the syncer crosses); (2) between "has text" and "knows of" (the width dial; `lazy-all`'s holes name the tests); (3) between a record and a rendered key (two waists, two grains; a key carries state a reader paints from nothing, and a key whose payload reads as an operation counts as a delta wearing a key); (4) between a port and an attachment (what fits in the attachment may hibernate); (5) between a human's act and a river's percept (both arrive as writes or verbs with an actor; only one passes a declared capability); (6) between a peer write and a focused control (the page keeps the field while its local revision exceeds the sensed one). What not to cut: TW5's core bytes and the integrity gate; the CRDT as truth; the language's host reading; refusal by name.

**Pentacle `_`.** Unclaimed: how incremental TW5's filter language can be made; the count and weight of worker-side verbs that need the language (F's census); whether a `worker_thread` starts from a user-land `v8.startupSnapshot`; the glass heap at skinny width; the serialised bytes per key for a 2,000-tiddler river once the river splits into frame keys; the peer-write-into-open-editor path (the navigator's draft logic, unread); whether `new Function` over a 2.2 MB core runs acceptably on Hermes or QuickJS; Mudlet's Qt label subset as rendered; whether the sensorium's actual dependencies admit any browser vessel; who re-pours the goldens when the engine commit moves.

**Arcana `0`.** "Which architecture should hold a portable TW5 engine?" dissolves twice. TW5 shipped two architectures for twelve years, the image and the server-client wiki, and every third way relocates the truth of one of them. Then the rulings dissolve the second half: the engine stays one JS evaluator; what ports reads as **rendered keys from any root over any document**, and the portability the house wants rides on the language's suite, not on moving the evaluator. The frame "portable engine" survives as "portable language with one reference evaluator, many cameras, and one lifecycle".

**Signal-Jam `*_`.** The visible feed says full width dissolves seven gaps and the field agrees; the hidden ground says the two-core cost and the skinny number both stand unmeasured. Committing to a full replica before the three-boot spike forecloses skinny for the price of two weeks. Drop the Wand; keep the Pentacle until §10 lands.

**Dubious-Move `?!`.** Macro says "C reads as E at full width" closes the question; micro says the two notches fail differently (full on memory, skinny on `lazy-all`'s holes, none on page-controls build cost), and a dial with three failure modes still needs three tests. Macro says the language carries portability; micro says a lean host receives a rendered key, which reads as a *projection* of the language, so the contract reaches it only as far as the camera's degradation rule holds. Keep the bet; write the camera goldens.

---

